{"id":"8290c214ec3c85ca","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-rademacher.md","title":"Rademacher Functions","display":"df-rademacher — Rademacher Functions","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-rademacher","aliases":["58-df-rademacher","Rademacher Functions"],"display":"df-rademacher — Rademacher Functions","depends_on":["[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-rademacher"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-rademacher</span><span>Rademacher Functions</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-rademacher — Rademacher Functions"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r\\in V\">\\(r\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"t\\in[0,1)\">\\(t\\in[0,1)\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RademacherSystem}_S(r)\">\\(\\mathrm{RademacherSystem}_S(r)\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>对 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\\in\\mathbb R\">\\(x\\in\\mathbb R\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lfloor x\\rfloor\\coloneqq\\iota k\\;(k\\in\\mathbb Z\\land k\\le x&lt;k+1)\">\\(\\lfloor x\\rfloor\\coloneqq\\iota k\\;(k\\in\\mathbb Z\\land k\\le x&lt;k+1)\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\iota\">\\(\\iota\\)</span> 表示唯一满足者。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}rademacher}\\vdash\\mathrm{RademacherSystem}_S(r)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1)\\;\\left(r(n)(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor}\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}rademacher}\\vdash\\mathrm{RademacherSystem}_S(r)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1)\\;\\left(r(n)(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor}\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Independence is a theorem after equipping <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[0,1)\">\\([0,1)\\)</span> with Lebesgue probability measure; it is not folded into the concrete function definition.</li>\n<li>Khintchine: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{E}[|\\sum a_n r_n|^p]^{1/p} \\asymp (\\sum a_n^2)^{1/2}\">\\(\\mathbb{E}[|\\sum a_n r_n|^p]^{1/p} \\asymp (\\sum a_n^2)^{1/2}\\)</span> for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p &gt; 0\">\\(p &gt; 0\\)</span></li>\n<li>Steinhaus: related <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varepsilon_n\">\\(\\varepsilon_n\\)</span> with uniform on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[0,1]\">\\([0,1]\\)</span></li>\n<li>Concentration: deviation bounds for Rademacher sums</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ledoux and Talagrand, Probability in Banach Spaces</li>\n<li>Kwapień and Woyczyński, Random Series and Trigonometric Integrals</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$r\\in V$ and $\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})$ (see [[58-df-function]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"r\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})","display":false},{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"t\\in[0,1)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RademacherSystem}_S(r)","display":false},{"tex":"x\\in\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\lfloor x\\rfloor\\coloneqq\\iota k\\;(k\\in\\mathbb Z\\land k\\le x<k+1)","display":false},{"tex":"\\iota","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}rademacher}\\vdash\\mathrm{RademacherSystem}_S(r)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1)\\;\\left(r(n)(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor}\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"[0,1)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb{E}[|\\sum a_n r_n|^p]^{1/p} \\asymp (\\sum a_n^2)^{1/2}","display":false},{"tex":"p > 0","display":false},{"tex":"\\varepsilon_n","display":false},{"tex":"[0,1]","display":false}],"bytes":1336,"backlinks":[{"id":"bee0665ec95eaa96","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1)\\;(r(n)(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor})$ (see [[../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md]], [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1028","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md|58-df-rademacher]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["36d7463d215be751"]}